<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38150" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπανα-τίθημι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lay upon,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαναθῶ σοι καὶ ξύλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					148
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <i>shift</i> a burden, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				4.286.7
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii/iv A.D.)</span>: —
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μείζων δύναμις ἐ. τινί</span>
			<i>is entrusted</i> to him, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				926d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>shift one's position,</i> of patients under
			operation, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(2).425
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>bequeath,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PLips.
				29.7
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>shut,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σανίδας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.535
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i>).</div>
